      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8487",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The notation \n\n$$\ng: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$ to the set $\\mathbb{R}.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\},$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039287/example-8487.json",
          "file_sha256": "6820ad0ea265f9cbda146c145bc5bd3c4ce1b40fdd604c373d4be2574f8e754a"
        }
